@startuml HermesCLIEditing
 title hermes-cli: document editing, recovery and conflicts
 top to bottom direction
 skinparam nodesep 45
 skinparam ranksep 60
 skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
 skinparam packageStyle rectangle
 hide empty members

package "Presentation" {
  class "CLI edit command" as CLI <<controller>>
  class "TUI document screen" as TUI <<controller>>
}
package "internal/app" {
  class "Documents" as Documents <<struct>> {
    BeginEdit(ctx, documentID): Draft
    SaveEdit(ctx, draftID): SaveResult
    CompareLatest(ctx, draftID): Comparison
    RebaseDraft(ctx, draftID, reviewedVersion): Draft
    DiscardDraft(ctx, draftID): error
  }
  interface "DocumentsRemote" as Remote {
    Get(ctx, documentID): Document
    Update(ctx, documentID, title, content, expectedVersion): Document
  }
  interface "DraftStore" as Store {
    Create(ctx, document): Draft
    Load(ctx, draftID): Draft
    SetBase(ctx, draftID, reviewedDocument): Draft
    Delete(ctx, draftID): error
  }
}
package "internal/model" {
  class "Document" as Doc <<data>> {
    ID
    WorkspaceID
    Title
    Content
    Version
  }
  class "Draft" as Draft <<data>> {
    ID
    ServerIdentity
    UserID
    DocumentID
    BaseVersion
    BaseTitle / BaseContent
    WorkingFilePath
    ProposedTitle
  }
  class "SaveResult" as Result <<data>> {
    outcome: saved / unchanged / conflict / unknown / failed
    document: optional
    recoveryPath: optional
    cleanupError: optional
  }
  class "Comparison" as Comparison <<data>> {
    base: Document snapshot
    local: draft text and title
    latest: Document
  }
}
package "internal/editor" {
  interface "Editor" as Editor {
    Edit(ctx, workingFilePath): error
  }
  class "SystemEditor" as SystemEditor <<struct>>
}
package "Adapters" {
  class "HTTPDocumentClient" as HTTPClient <<struct>>
  class "GRPCDocumentClient" as GRPCClient <<struct>>
  class "FileDraftStore" as Files <<struct>>
}

package "Test doubles (test code only)" {
  class "FakeDocumentClient" as FakeClient <<struct>>
}

CLI -down-> Documents
TUI -down-> Documents
CLI --> Editor : foreground process
TUI --> Editor : suspend UI; run editor; resume UI
Documents -down-> Remote
Documents -down-> Store
Documents ..> Result
Documents ..> Comparison
Store ..> Draft
Remote ..> Doc
HTTPClient ..|> Remote
GRPCClient ..|> Remote
FakeClient ..|> Remote
Files ..|> Store
SystemEditor ..|> Editor
Draft --> Doc : base snapshot
Comparison --> Draft : local revision

note right of Remote
  Protocol-independent operations using application models/errors.
  HTTP and gRPC are alternative adapters selected at bootstrap.
  Tests inject FakeDocumentClient for deterministic error scenarios.
end note
note left of Documents
  BeginEdit:
  1. Load document and its version from server.
  2. Persist base snapshot and editable Markdown file.
  3. Return draft only after local persistence succeeds.

  SaveEdit:
  1. Load draft metadata and edited file.
  2. Verify server/account matches the draft.
  3. Submit changes with BaseVersion.
  4. Clean up only after confirmed save or explicit discard.
  No terminal I/O or external editor process in this struct.
end note
note right of Editor
  Edits an existing persistent draft file.
  Editor failure or cancellation retains the draft.
  Editor does not upload content or delete recovery files.
  Presentation decides when terminal ownership changes.
end note
note right of Result
  Conflict: preserve file and offer manual comparison.
  Unknown network outcome: retain file; inspect latest document.
  No automatic retry or unconditional overwrite.
  Lost access: retain file but do not expose new remote content.
  Cleanup failure after save is reported separately from save failure.
end note
note bottom of Comparison
  CompareLatest retrieves current content only if access still exists.
  RebaseDraft is explicit after the user reviews/merges against latest:
  update the base snapshot/version; preserve the working content.
  Another concurrent update can still cause a new conflict on SaveEdit.
  No automatic merge is assumed.
end note
note bottom of Files
  Persist drafts before launching editor; use owner-only file access.
  Give concurrent edits distinct draft IDs and working files.
  Keep drafts across process exits; scope them to server and user.
  A working file survives until confirmed save or explicit discard.
end note
legend bottom
  Proposed contracts, not final Go signatures.
  ctx represents context.Context for cancellation and request deadlines.
  Interfaces are implemented by adapters; application logic is shared by CLI and TUI.
endlegend
@enduml
